<%# The story glass (owner's choice, November 2026): a glass that fills as the
    reader scrolls through the homepage story, empty at the first step and
    full at the closing beat ("That's the whole ritual."). Driven by
    story_glass_controller.js.

    The drawing is shared/_glass at full, its level lowered by the controller
    (the liquid is translated down, as in the pour). It is a gauge, so it
    stays out of the appear controller's pour.
    - Desktop (900px and up): a 96px gauge in the gutter between the step
      words and the face, held at the middle of the screen while the steps
      pass. Sticky with no height, so it takes no space. The step words keep
      a clear margin from it (.beat padding in home/index), and the faces sit
      in their own column, so it never meets either.
    - Phones and tablets: 40px in the bottom-right corner, in the page's
      20px gutter (only the glass's transparent margin reaches past it), so
      it never covers text, the nav or a tap target. Shown only while the
      steps are on screen.
    - aria-hidden, no words, lets every tap through. Hidden until its
      controller connects (no JS, no glass), hidden in print. Under reduced
      motion the level does not follow the scroll: it steps a third at a
      time as each step is reached, with no motion. %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%# Its styles: app/assets/stylesheets/home/story_glass.css (no inline <style>: the CSP, issue #46). %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "home/story_glass" %>
<% end %>
<div class="story-glass" data-controller="story-glass" hidden aria-hidden="true">
  <%= render "shared/glass", level: 1, size: 96, appear: false %>
</div>
